Z||000005||Coop88||08-22-2000||12:05 PM||||Thanks for the info!! I put on an AC Delco coil and the car is MUCH more responsive. I had no idea the old one was that bad. Just gotta get that new cat welded in place.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||Alex4mula||08-22-2000||01:41 PM||||My Accell had last longer than my AC Delco and has better spark energy. Just for you to have a better population sample.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||08-22-2000||04:42 PM||||Im a victim of not taking my own advice!<P>I was in a jam and bought an after market coil just to get my Fiero back on the road. Forgot about until 3 months later (last week.) I was kidding around with a friend and hit a curving freeway onramp, (Ramp was a tight right hand downward curve going under the overpass.) I had her hard in the corner when POP! The coil gave out, put my car into a drop throttle oversteer and started skidding sideways towards a very unfriendly looking lightpole. I stopped within about a yard of it. It started up again and I hobbled it all the way home. Feeling the humiliation of knowing what I did wrong and having 4 tires with flat spots on them...<P>The next day I was at the dealer getting an AC Delco coil!<P>GO AC Delco or TOW home!||||reg||4
Z||000008||HugGRRRFiero||08-22-2000||05:33 PM||||  ACDelco has a long long history in my area, so I like to buy Genuine ACDelco parts as much as I can.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
